%description:

Tcp.retainSackAfterRto:clear -- after a timeout, host1 sends the SACKed data again.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "false: a retransmission timeout clears the SACKed marks of the
scoreboard (RFC 2018 section 8, RFC 5682 step 1); true: the marks survive the timeout, as Linux
keeps them".

The classes: clear (false, the default) and retain (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
at a timeout, TcpAlgorithmBase::processRexmitTimer() clears the SACKed marks of the
retransmission queue unless the value is true; after the timeout, TcpConnection::sendSegment()
skips the data with a SACKed mark. This test separates "clear" from "retain".

Host under test: host1, with an initial window of 4 segments and without the tail loss probe
(preconditions), which sends four segments; the round trip is 40 ms. The tap drops each transmission of the first
and the third segment in the first 0.5 s; host2 SACKs the second and the fourth segment, and
the timer of host1 expires. After the timeout, the tap hides the SACK blocks of host2 (NOP
options of the same length), so the marks of before the timeout are the only knowledge of
host1 about the fourth segment. Observation: level 1, after the timeout, host1 sends the fourth segment again.

%# parameter: Tcp.retainSackAfterRto
%# class: clear
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.retainSackAfterRto
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpRetainSackAfterRtoClear")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("(tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 || tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 2896) && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").drop().within(0.5)
                     .describe("each transmission of the first and the third data segment of host1 in the first 0.5 s"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("numRtos").describe("the timeout of host1").within(3.0))
        .meanwhile(tap("tap").from("host2").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false").mutate([](Packet *frame) { hideTcpOption(frame, inet::tcp::TCPOPTION_SACK); })
                       .describe("each ACK of host2 after the timeout: the SACK blocks hidden"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 4344 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the fourth segment again, in the go-back-N after the timeout")
             .within(2.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpRetainSackAfterRtoClear compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.retainSackAfterRto = false    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 5792B
*.host1.tcp.initialCwnd = 4
*.host1.tcp.tlpEnabled = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpRetainSackAfterRtoClear: PASS
